310: ## Owner decision D8 — T1 review finding 1 (2026-10-07)
311: 
312: Asked (native question UI, pt-BR) for the deployed git ref and a read-only online count of participants without a
313: conversation_members row. Owner, verbatim: "O aplicativo nao tem acesso por ninguem online, somente eu e uns 
amigos
314: acessamos no momento, então nao se preocupe". Recorded as accepted risk: an older hosted build that authorizes via
315: conversations.participants may get an error marking read for a participant whose member row was deleted, until the
316: Phase 5 app is deployed. No online read performed. AC-034's hosted-build smoke (T21) still needs the owner's git 
ref.
317: 
318: ## Owner decision D9 — conversation_members self-enrollment gap (2026-10-07)
319: 
320: Discovered by the T4 performer and verified by the orchestrator on LOCAL: baseline policies on 
`public.conversation_members`
321: ("Users can insert their own conversation preferences" WITH CHECK only user_id = caller; "Users can update their 
own
322: conversation preferences" with no WITH CHECK) plus INSERT/UPDATE grants to anon/authenticated let an 
authenticated user
323: add themselves to any conversation, or move their own row to another conversation, through the Data API. That 
defeats every
324: members-only rule (messages, attachments, receipts, mentions, roster, typing topic). App code does not need these 
client
325: writes: memberships come from the SECURITY DEFINER trigger `sync_conversation_members`, and the 
preferences/archive routes
326: write with the service-role client after `requireConversationParticipant`.
327: Asked (native question UI, pt-BR) whether to fix it in this phase. Owner chose: "Corrigir nesta fase 
(Recomendado)" — a new
328: task with a migration removing client creation/move of memberships, applied online with the others at T23, under 
the PLAN
329: and task review gates. To be planned as a replan (new task ID T28) after T4 closes.
330: 
